   "source": [
    "# Regolith Dielectric Map — S1 Week 2\n",
    "\n",
    "Lunar regolith dielectric properties and their effect on a communication link.\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook covers:\n",
    "1. Loss tangent vs frequency for three regolith densities\n",
    "2. Permittivity / loss tangent / skin depth summary across bands\n",
    "3. Key number: how much the tan d = 0 (Edwards 2023) assumption underestimates loss at S-band\n",
    "4. South Pole DEM context (Connecting Ridge, Shackleton rim)\n",
    "\n",
    "Models implemented in `lunarcomms.regolith.dielectric`:\n",
    "- Permittivity: eps' = 1.919^rho  (Olhoeft & Strangway 1975)\n",
    "- Loss tangent: tan d = 10^(0.312 rho - 2.636) * f_GHz^0.278  (Siegler et al. 2020)\n",
    "- Skin depth: delta_s = lambda0 / (pi * sqrt(eps') * tan d)  (Ulaby & Long 2014)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "59cff274",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "\n",
    "from lunarcomms.regolith.dielectric import (\n",
    "    permittivity, loss_tangent, complex_permittivity, skin_depth_m\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "%matplotlib inline\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8a2f1bfc",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Loss tangent vs frequency (three densities)\n",
    "\n",
    "The required deliverable: tan d versus frequency for three representative regolith densities, with the UHF / S / Ka bands marked."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "id": "417ee99f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 900x600 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "freqs = np.logspace(np.log10(0.4), np.log10(37), 300)   # GHz\n",
    "densities = [1.30, 1.50, 1.74]                          # surface / upper / deep regolith\n",
    "labels = [\"rho = 1.30 (surface)\", \"rho = 1.50 (upper 30 cm)\", \"rho = 1.74 (deep)\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(9, 6))\n",
    "for rho, lab in zip(densities, labels):\n",
    "    ax.loglog(freqs, loss_tangent(rho, freqs), lw=2, label=lab)\n",
    "\n",
    "for fb, name in [(0.44, \"UHF\"), (2.5, \"S\"), (8.4, \"X\"), (27.0, \"Ka\")]:\n",
    "    ax.axvline(fb, color=\"grey\", ls=\":\", alpha=0.6)\n",
    "    ax.text(fb, ax.get_ylim()[0], \" \" + name, color=\"grey\", va=\"bottom\", fontsize=9)\n",
    "\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel(\"Frequency (GHz)\")\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel(\"Loss tangent  tan d\")\n",
    "ax.set_title(\"Lunar regolith loss tangent vs frequency\")\n",
    "ax.grid(True, which=\"both\", alpha=0.3)\n",
    "ax.legend()\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "caa922ba",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Loss tangent rises with both **frequency** (the f^0.278 power law, from ilmenite dissipation) and **density** (the 0.312*rho term). Higher bands and denser regolith are lossier."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "15c188e7",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Permittivity, loss tangent, and skin depth across bands\n",
    "\n",
    "At the nominal upper-layer density rho = 1.50 g/cm^3."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "id": "946e02fb",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Band    f (GHz)   eps_prime       tan d  skin depth (m)\n",
      "-------------------------------------------------------\n",
      "UHF        0.44       2.658     0.00541          24.605\n",
      "S          2.50       2.658     0.00876           2.672\n",
      "X          8.40       2.658     0.01227           0.568\n",
      "Ka        27.00       2.658     0.01698           0.128\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "rho = 1.50\n",
    "print(f\"{'Band':<6}{'f (GHz)':>9}{'eps_prime':>12}{'tan d':>12}{'skin depth (m)':>16}\")\n",
    "print(\"-\" * 55)\n",
    "for name, f in [(\"UHF\", 0.44), (\"S\", 2.5), (\"X\", 8.4), (\"Ka\", 27.0)]:\n",
    "    print(f\"{name:<6}{f:>9.2f}{permittivity(rho):>12.3f}\"\n",
    "          f\"{loss_tangent(rho, f):>12.5f}{skin_depth_m(rho, f):>16.3f}\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d92d66b6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Skin depth shrinks sharply with frequency: metres at UHF/S-band, centimetres by Ka-band. This is why low frequencies are used for subsurface sounding and high frequencies are surface-only."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "42d30582",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Key number: the tan d = 0 assumption at S-band\n",
    "\n",
    "Edwards et al. (2023) use tan d = 0 (lossless). The dielectric absorption over a path L is\n",
    "\n",
    "    Loss_dB = 8.686 * L / delta_s\n",
    "\n",
    "(one skin depth = 1 neper of field = 8.686 dB of power). Computed for rho = 1.50, f = 2.5 GHz.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "id": "ee2304a9",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "skin depth          : 2.672 m\n",
      "dielectric loss rate: 3.251 dB/m\n",
      "loss over 10 km     : 32,510 dB  (with real tan d)\n",
      "loss with tan d = 0 : 0 dB  (Edwards 2023)\n",
      "--> underestimate   : 32,510 dB over 10 km\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "rho, f, L = 1.50, 2.5, 10_000.0  # 10 km path, in metres\n",
    "ds = skin_depth_m(rho, f)\n",
    "loss_per_m = 8.686 / ds\n",
    "loss_total = 8.686 * L / ds\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"skin depth          : {ds:.3f} m\")\n",
    "print(f\"dielectric loss rate: {loss_per_m:.3f} dB/m\")\n",
    "print(f\"loss over 10 km     : {loss_total:,.0f} dB  (with real tan d)\")\n",
    "print(f\"loss with tan d = 0 : 0 dB  (Edwards 2023)\")\n",
    "print(f\"--> underestimate   : {loss_total:,.0f} dB over 10 km\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4cafd2a6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Interpretation.** The skin depth at S-band is only ~2.7 m, so the dielectric loss rate is ~3.25 dB/m. Lunar regolith blocks S-band within a few metres.\n",
    "\n",
    "- For a **vacuum surface link** (signal travels above the regolith), the tan d = 0 assumption is fine — the wave barely interacts with the medium.\n",
    "- For any **subsurface or grazing path through regolith**, ignoring tan d is severe: even a few metres of regolith costs ~10 dB that Edwards (2023) omits.\n",
    "\n",
    "The 10 km figure is illustrative — you would never propagate that far *through* regolith at S-band; the meaningful quantity is the **per-metre rate (~3.25 dB/m)** equivalently stated as the **2.7 m skin depth**.\n",
    "\n",
    "*Note: the loss_tangent docstring's \"~0.3-0.6 dB/km\" hint corresponds to a different (mostly-vacuum) scenario, not the skin-depth-through-medium calculation here.*\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "56bd7035",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. South Pole DEM context\n",
    "\n",
    "The two scenario sites from PGDA-78 (LRO/LOLA, 5 m/pixel): Connecting Ridge (Site01) and Shackleton rim (Site04)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "id": "bad72597",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1400x600 with 4 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from lunarcomms.io.pgda import load_dem\n",
    "\n",
    "def find_dem(site):\n",
    "    for base in [Path(\"data/dem\"), Path(\"../data/dem\")]:\n",
    "        p = base / site / f\"{site}_final_adj_5mpp_surf.tif\"\n",
    "        if p.exists():\n",
    "            return str(p)\n",
    "    raise FileNotFoundError(f\"DEM for {site} not found - run data/download_pgda.py\")\n",
    "\n",
    "sites = [(\"Site01\", \"Connecting Ridge\"), (\"Site04\", \"Shackleton rim\")]\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(14, 6))\n",
    "for ax, (site, label) in zip(axes, sites):\n",
    "    data, transform, crs = load_dem(find_dem(site))\n",
    "    half_km = (data.shape[0] * abs(transform.a)) / 1000.0 / 2.0\n",
    "    extent = [-half_km, half_km, -half_km, half_km]\n",
    "    im = ax.imshow(data, cmap=\"terrain\", extent=extent, origin=\"upper\")\n",
    "    ax.set_title(f\"{label} ({site})\")\n",
    "    ax.set_xlabel(\"East-West (km)\")\n",
    "    ax.set_ylabel(\"North-South (km)\")\n",
    "    ax.annotate(label, xy=(0, 0), xytext=(0, half_km * 0.6), ha=\"center\",\n",
    "                fontsize=10, fontweight=\"bold\",\n",
    "                arrowprops=dict(arrowstyle=\"->\"))\n",
    "    fig.colorbar(im, ax=ax, label=\"Elevation (m)\", shrink=0.8)\n",
    "fig.suptitle(\"PGDA-78 LOLA South Pole DEMs (5 m/pixel)\")\n",
    "fig.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5e4c26f1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Summary\n",
    "\n",
    "- Loss tangent and skin depth depend strongly on frequency and density.\n",
    "- At S-band, regolith skin depth ~2.7 m (loss ~3.25 dB/m); the tan d = 0 assumption is only valid for vacuum surface links.\n",
    "- The DEM sites provide the terrain context for the reflection/multipath geometry studied in later weeks.\n"
   ]
  }
